* "Windows" is a trademark owned by MicroSoft Corp.
$FG$


$FG,4$$WW,1$$TX+CX,"Possible Damnations"$$FG$

The compiler's parser makes RISC code which it optimizes to CISC.  This does not matter much, because the CPU converts it back to RISC and schedules it, internally.  An AntichristOS zealot with more zeal than us might say we should save lines-of-code by removing the CISC optimizing.  We would say: get thee behind us, and bring a benchmark.

Someday the compiler may learn to play a whole source file backwards.  Until then, use $FG,2$backwards$FG$ one string at a time.
